      "side": 1,
      "message": "FWIW I think this code now has too many layers. The original design only had two: OffloadController and OffloadHardwareInterface. OffloadController had the control logic, and OffloadHardwareInterface was a very simple class, with basically no state, which just converted the function calls to HIDL calls (including the HIDL synchronous callback boilerplate).\n\nThis CL keeps OffloadHardwareInterface and adds moves the actual code down to another layer (the HIDL/AIDL layer). That results in a lot of method duplication between the hardware interface and the HIDL impl (and, consequently, between the hardware interface and the AIDL impl).\n\nIt seems like it would have been better to essentially rename OffloadHardwareInterface to the HIDL impl, and move the few bits of non-HIDL code into OffloadController.\n\nIt\u0027s probably too late to change the design at this stage, and this code doesn\u0027t change very often so readability isn\u0027t super important. But we should at least remove the code duplication (e.g., the duplication of identical log messages).",
      "revId": "403076a4d245d2e2ad8021c3562a2a3c83bf36f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
