      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T10:26:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This CL contains dozens of lines of boilerplate like this. This doesn\u0027t seem useful because all the handle*Exception methods are basically the same anyway. None of them actually do anything, they just log. If that\u0027s what we want, then it\u0027s much simpler to do something like:\n\n    public boolean stopOffload() {\n        final String methodStr \u003d \"stopOffload\";\n        try {\n            mIOffload.stopOffload();\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            logAndIgnoreException(e, methodStr);\n            return false;\n        }\n        mTetheringOffloadCallback \u003d null;\n        return true;     \n    }\n\n    private void logAndIgnoreException(Exception e) {\n        mLog.e(\"IOffload.\" + methodStr + \" failed with + \" e.getClass().getSimpleName() + \": \", e);\n    }\n\nActually, I\u0027m not even sure you need the getClass().getSimpleName() because the log likely already prints the exception class. Probably a good idea to check though.\n\nIf you do this the behaviour will be a bit different from the what\u0027s in this CL right now, because this CL catches different types of exceptions in different calls. For example, stopOffload catches IllegalStateException, RemoteException and ServiceSpecificException, but it does not catch IllegalArgumentException. I think the only difference is that the code in this CL right now will crash the networkstack process (and the system) if we get an exception we don\u0027t expect, whereas what I suggest here will just ignore the exception and log.\n\nIf you really want to catch different exceptions in different methods, and crash if you get an exception of a different type, you can always do that with:\n\n        try {\n            mIOffload.stopOffload();\n        } catch (IllegalStateException | RemoteException | ServiceSpecificException e) {\n            logAndIgnoreException(e);\n            return false;\n        }",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 99,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 108,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "403076a4d245d2e2ad8021c3562a2a3c83bf36f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
