      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T10:26:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is very hard to read. See go/tott/455 for why this is bad.\n\nCan you unindent? Something like the following:\n\n    if (h1 \u003d\u003d null || h2 \u003d\u003d null) {\n        mLog.e(\"Failed to create socket\");\n        maybeCloseFdInNativeHandle(h1);\n        maybeCloseFdInNativeHandle(h2);\n        return OFFLOAD_HAL_VERSION_NONE;\n    }\n\n    requestSocketDump(h1);\n    ...\n    if (!mIOffload.initOffload(h1, h2, mOffloadHalCallback)) {\n        mIOffload.stopOffload();\n        mLog.e(\"Failed to initialize offload.\");\n        maybeCloseFdInNativeHandle(h1);\n        maybeCloseFdInNativeHandle(h2);\n        return OFFLOAD_HAL_VERSION_NONE;\n    }\n\n    // Explicitly close FDs for HIDL. AIDL will pass the original FDs to the service,\n    // they shouldn\u0027t be closed here.\n    if (mIOffload.getVersion() \u003c OFFLOAD_HAL_VERSION_AIDL) {\n        maybeCloseFdInNativeHandle(h1);\n        maybeCloseFdInNativeHandle(h2);\n    }\n    return mIOffload.getVersion();\n\n\nIf the duplication of calls to maybeCloseFdInNativeHandle bothers you, you could use a helper method to reduce that. Also, given that you always close the fds together, then maybe add a method that closes both of them?\n\n    private void maybeCloseFdInNativeHandles(final NativeHandle... handles) {\n        for (NativeHandle h : handles) {\n            if (h \u003d\u003d null) continue;\n            try {\n                h.close();\n            } catch (IOException | IllegalStateException e) {\n                // IllegalStateException means fd is already closed, do nothing here.\n                // Also nothing we can do if IOException.\n            }\n        }\n    }",
      "range": {
