      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T10:26:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this code needed? Do we need to support calling getForwardedStats if there is no offload HAL? It seems confusing to return empty stats if we don\u0027t have a pointer to the HAL.\n\nThe previous code didn\u0027t do that. If getForwardedStats was called with a null mOffloadControl, it would crash with an NPE. Presumably that means that this can never happen. If so, we should remove the null check.\n\nLooks like you have similar null checks in all the other methods, so maybe remove all of them? Or more specifically, remove all the ones that didn\u0027t already exist.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 356,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 356,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "403076a4d245d2e2ad8021c3562a2a3c83bf36f4",
